  "summary": "Built block content in GFM table cells in the working tree (uncommitted): encodeLine and decodeLine on the Markdown mapping contexts, implemented in markdownLine.ts, write a cell on one line (lists as main's inline <ul>/<ol start>/<li> HTML, other blocks collapsed or dropped with reports, no raw line ending or row-splitting |) and read it back, with list runs built by the installed List decoders. Table cells call them, merged cells flatten through the table grid with a 100,000-cell bound, the paragraph decoder keeps a trailing break before <br>, list items keep bare URLs, tag attributes escape |, and the reference passes filter by type. Docs, editor-behavior law, the decision page, the changeset and the API manifest updated.",
